Report a write error on standard output when awk exits.
awk_exit() ended with exit(), which flushes standard output without
checking, so awk's output was lost without a message or a failure
status when it could not be written, as with "awk '{ print }' file
>/dev/full". Exit through fflush_stdout_and_exit() instead, which keeps
the status of an exit statement when there is no error.

---
 editors/awk.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/editors/awk.c
+++ b/editors/awk.c
@@ -4145,7 +4145,7 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	exit(G.exitcode);
+	fflush_stdout_and_exit(G.exitcode);
 }
 
 int awk_main(int argc, char **argv) MAIN_EXTERNALLY_VISIBLE;
